    psi: execute descriptor-indexed private ranks end to end (#824)
    
    * psi: retain descriptor bounds on indexed entry coordinates
    
    Entry coordinate geometry distinguishes fixed-array extents from live descriptor observations. Literal slice selectors retain runtime index obligations, with exact collection prefixes and independently proved entry bounds. The unchanged seven/empty private-cycle witness is refused by the fixed d837145 baseline; this checkpoint retains the repair for focused execution validation.
    
    * psi: transport finite collection observations through windows
    
    Array construction retains completed scalar coordinates. Builtin windows translate their finite observations using the same independently checked endpoint decision as descriptor lengths; a dynamic selection joins an equal-valued contiguous run only with its own inclusion proof. Preserve the frozen private-rank witness and carry it across nine transport places with strict-descent reject twins.
    
    * psi: preserve collection snapshots and joined scalar bounds
    
    Completed match values retain the union of independently captured arm bounds. Finite element observations can then prove a dynamic selection without assuming an arm. Borrowed captures retain their original source coordinates before window rebasing; owned copies retain independent value semantics.
    
    * psi: trace descriptor contract captures during diagnosis
    
    * psi: retain mathematical bounds for completed scalar joins
    
    Anonymous literal arms have integer values before any executable carrier reference is selected. Preserve their proved bounds on the completed join instead of requiring an unrelated type reference. Remove temporary capture tracing after it identified the precise loss; array and window observations were already retained correctly.
    
    * psi: transport aggregate result observations through public contracts
    
    Completed aggregate results retain exact typed scalar coordinates. The shared independent call-guarantee owner binds those observations without inspecting a callee body or granting bounds from geometry. Current value capture transports fields through every join predecessor and carries checked constructor carriers for anonymous array elements. The frozen nine-place descriptor rank programs remain unchanged.
    
    * psi: keep aggregate result observations on owned snapshots
    
    Returned references require independent binding and load custody; the new aggregate result roster admits only owned inline scalar coordinates. Duplicate source occurrences bind the same snapshot while each coordinate is installed only once.
    
    * psi: retain result facts through assignments and value joins
    
    Aggregate completion uses the selected machine result namespace independently of its arithmetic entry-state telescope. Assignment imports the same guarantees as initialization at the captured destination cut. Value joins retain alternative source coordinates separately, adding them as live backing dependencies only for borrowed results.
    
    * omega: form element views through retained pointer regions
    
    A matched reference carries an address word. Collection view formation resolves every pointer region before its final collection offset and selectors, reusing the shared address walk. Target admission reconstructs the retained path and access ceiling; native selection loads the actual stored pointer rather than descriptor bytes. Collection and establishment queries move under their operation owners.
    
    * omega: retain descriptor refusal ownership after module extraction
    
    * omega: retain reference access ceilings on view formation
    
    Readable pointer geometry does not grant mutable access. Establishment lowering and target admission now use the same full descriptor-path authority query as selection, with the actual root declaration and requested access.
    
    * compiler: retain typed backing authority across descriptor producers
    
    Descriptor lineage metadata no longer rejects every stored-reference path. The shared typed backing-access owner validates every establishment/subslice hop against its actual source declaration and full access ceiling, rejecting cycles and duplicate producers. All access consumers fail closed when this join is unavailable. Pin the unchanged nine descriptor-rank programs and strict twins, plus literal, assignment, copy and bound controls, for source-to-native qualification.
    
    * omega: use typed backing authority for descriptor transfers
    
    Structural transfer admission consumes the shared source-chain authority result rather than inferring mutable backing from affine multiplicity. Owned carrier custody remains separate from lending its payload.
    
    * omega: admit typed reference paths in descriptor selection
    
    The legalized descriptor source query already intersects every stored reference ceiling with its actual root authority. Remove the earlier blanket Referent refusal so the typed path decision owns admission.
    
